MATH LAB
Local Lab Facilitator Handbook
A practical guide to launching, organizing, and leading your own Math Lab
One Investigation → Multiple Levels → Shared Discovery.
Welcome to Math Lab! This handbook will help you establish a Local Lab in your community, connect with participants, organize your first session, and create an environment where people can explore mathematics together.
You do not need to be an expert in every area of mathematics, have a large budget, or develop an entire curriculum before getting started. You need a place to meet, an interest in helping people explore mathematics, and a willingness to learn alongside your participants.
This handbook provides the steps, examples, and resources to help you get started.
