Final Thoughts
Math Lab is built around the idea that mathematical discovery can happen at many levels and that people benefit from exploring ideas together.
As a Local Lab facilitator, you help make that experience possible in your community.
You do not need to have every answer. You need to create opportunities for participants to ask questions, test ideas, explain their reasoning, and discover new mathematical connections.
Choose topics that interest your audience, adapt your activities to different levels of mathematical depth, and make room for participants to develop their own approaches.
At the same time, stay connected to the broader Math Lab network by participating in the monthly National Investigation, working toward a group solution, and sharing your experiences and feedback.
One Investigation → Multiple Levels → Shared Discovery.
Thank you for helping Math Lab grow.
